Mace or hammer are good ways to go for priest but unless
you spend an early wish on the Sceptre of Might as a
lawfull or get Mjollnir as a neutral, it's hardly worth it once
another good artifact weapon comes up.  Ogresmasher or
Trollsbane?  Not worth it.  Werebane may be worth
unrestricting saber skill slot and is nicer to enchant than
a non-artifact saber for a class who can't two weapon,
but generally with a priest I want to go with gifted weapons.

> If it matters, I ate a bunch of wraiths on the Quest and am at level
> 30, and I have one guaranteed wish still available (the wrest wish
> from the Castle wand). =A0AC's around -22.

Bow to basic to have some sort of reasonable missile
strategy.  Create familiar spell to spam levels with pets as
the closest to an attack spell available.  Whatever attack
spells that happen to show up.

I favor Stormy as one of the top artifact weapons in the
game.  Level draining is more powerful than any of the
tables show, even though some of the nastiest monsters
in the game are immune to it.  Strormy is good enough that
as a wizard I like to altar dance trying for +FoD to be able
to get it at crowning.

Missile - bow.  Spell - whatever attack comes available
plus creating pets as a shield.  Stormy for melee.


